cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use myconote-cli in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "myconote-cli: Blazing-fast genome annotation pipeline"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-04-09
authors:
  - family-names: "Narh-Madey"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
    email: "narhmadey@wisc.edu"
    affiliation: "Hittinger Lab, Laboratory of Genetics, University of Wisconsin-Madison"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/K-nie/myconote-cli"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genome annotation
  - gene prediction
  - fungi
  - mycology
  - phylogenetics
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  myconote-cli is a high-performance genome annotation pipeline written
  in Rust, designed for eukaryotic genomes with particular strength in
  fungal biology. It integrates 30+ bioinformatics tools for gene
  prediction, functional annotation, comparative genomics, and NCBI
  submission preparation, all accessible through a single CLI.
